DO Resolve ticket_id, absolute project, private absolute ix/acli, and absolute assets under shared
    Inux guidance from ../assets
    beside this program. Let ix own directory/template validation, snapshots, and initialization
    (plain directories supported; linked Git worktrees unsupported). No separate inspections,
    listings/hashes, template reads/copies, or CLI/PR/conversion lookup; keep local steps quiet.

SHELL `{ix} task --snapshot {project}` AS snapshot_result

SET state = JSON(stdout of snapshot_result)

CHECK state is ok

SET snapshot = snapshot of state

SHELL `{acli} jira workitem view {ticket_id} --fields key,issuetype,summary,status,assignee,description,attachment --json` AS jira_result

SET ticket = JSON(stdout of jira_result)

CHECK key of ticket == ticket_id

CHECK Requested ticket details are complete.

SET ticket_layout = """
# TICKET-ID

Type: <type>
Summary: <summary>
Status: <status>
Assignee: <assignee or None>

## Description

<full description or None>

## Criteria

<explicit criteria or None>

## Attachments

- <filename> — <URL>
"""

DO Prepare ticket_markdown in memory from ticket using ticket_layout: preserve full
    descriptions/lists/tables and media links with supplied names/URLs. Keep unresolved references,
    invent no mappings/criteria, and use None for absent values/attachments. Write nothing yet.

SHELL `{ix} task --expect {snapshot} {assets} {project}` AS workspace_result

SET workspace = JSON(stdout of workspace_result)

CHECK workspace is ok

CHECK files of workspace lists ticket.md, estimate.md, and pr.md.

SET directory = directory of workspace

DO Write ticket_markdown to returned directory's empty ticket.md. CLI replacement plus write finish
    the action; preserve Git exclusions/.gitignore, without copies/readback/final filesystem checks.

PRINT with ticket_id and three absolute file paths, briefly.
